                <pb facs="0222" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg124"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002 Manchuria/129: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-06-30T18:00:00+08:00">June 30, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 30—4:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>319. Supplementing my June 30, 5 p.m., the Inspector General ordered the
                    Commissioner to come to Shanghai in order that he might be saved embarrassment
                    but he refused presumably at the instance of the chief of the section of Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
                <p>Not repeated to the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
